sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2025-wisdom-20> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Applied systemically, the same bioelectric-modifying drug (monensin) triggers tail regeneration at tail wounds and leg regeneration at leg wounds, showing that the specificity of the regenerative response lies in the responding cell collective rather than in the reagent.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The same electroceutical, monensin, induces tails at tail wounds and legs at leg wounds";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Multiscale Wisdom of the Body: Collective Intelligence as a Tractable Interface for Next-Generation Biomedicine”, BioEssays : news and reviews in molecular, cellular and developmental biology (2025), doi:10.1002/bies.202400196; section “Applications and a Roadmap Toward a Radical Regenerative Medicine › Top‐Down Control Exploits Agential Materials by Pushing Complexity from the Engineer onto the System Itself”. Scope: Amphibian (Xenopus) tadpole tail and limb regeneration (author's lab's prior work, refs [128, 200])"
}
